# Circadian Biology & Metabolic Resilience
#
# Photic entrainment, sleep glymphatic clearance, GLUT4 glucose disposal, mitochondrial bioenergetics, and electrolytes.

#>spw_cache_physio_circadian_metabolic
#:cache #!physio_dev
#:layer #!pragmatics

^"intent"{
  ~#goal: "Model the biophysical rhythms, cellular bioenergetics, and electro-chemical gradients that sustain human metabolic flexibility and longevity."
  ~#mechanisms: "SCN photic entrainment, glymphatic neuro-cleansing, insulin-independent GLUT4 disposal, mitohormesis, and Na/K-ATPase transport"
}

^["circadian_photic_entrainment_and_melanopsin"]{
  biological_clock: "The central master pacemaker in the Suprachiasmatic Nucleus (SCN) governing peripheral cellular clocks in liver, muscle, and gut."
  light_protocols: #[
    "Morning Lux Threshold: Direct outdoor sunlight (10,000-100,000 lux) within 60 minutes of waking stimulating retinal melanopsin (ipRGCs)",
    "Cortisol Awakening Response (CAR): Photic signaling driving a sharp, healthy morning spike in cortisol and core body temperature",
    "Melatonin Protection at Dusk: Eliminating high-intensity blue photons (< 500 nm) 2 hours before sleep to allow uninhibited pineal melatonin synthesis",
    "Dark Bedroom Environment: Absolute dark (< 1 lux) during sleep to preserve parasympathetic tone and nighttime metabolic rest"
  ]
}

^["sleep_architecture_and_glymphatic_clearance"]{
  restorative_cycles: "Alternating cycles of Slow-Wave Sleep (N3) and Rapid Eye Movement (REM) sleep across 90-minute ultradian oscillations."
  neurochemical_processes: .{
    glymphatic_flush: "During N3 deep sleep, astrocytic aquaporin-4 (AQP4) channels expand interstitial space by 60%, flushing CSF through brain parenchyma"
    waste_clearance: "Removal of metabolic neurotoxins including amyloid-beta monomers, hyperphosphorylated tau, and alpha-synuclein"
    rem_affective_reset: "Noradrenergic silence during REM allowing emotional memory processing and somatic trauma de-potentiation"
  }[reg=facet]
}

^["metabolic_flexibility_and_glucose_disposal"]{
  definition: "The ability of skeletal muscle and liver to transition seamlessly between lipid beta-oxidation and carbohydrate glycolysis based on availability."
  pathways: #[
    "Insulin-Independent GLUT4 Translocation: Vigorous skeletal muscle contraction directly mobilizes glucose transporters to cell surfaces without insulin",
    "Postprandial Ambulation: A 15-minute walk immediately following a meal blunts glycemic excursion peaks by 30-50%",
    "Visceral Adiposity Reversal: Mitigating ectopic fat deposition in liver and pancreas to restore native beta-cell insulin secretory pulsatility"
  ]
}

^["mitochondrial_bioenergetics_and_mitohormesis"]{
  powerhouse_resilience: "Mitochondrial quality control governed by balanced biogenesis (PGC-1alpha) and targeted mitophagy (PINK1/Parkin)."
  mitohormetic_stimuli: #[
    "Zone 2 Aerobic Base: Sustained low-intensity cardiovascular work expanding mitochondrial volume density and fatty acid oxidation enzymes",
    "Thermal Conditioning (Sauna): Heat shock proteins (HSP70) preventing protein misfolding and boosting human growth hormone secretion",
    "Cold Thermogenesis: Norepinephrine surge stimulating uncoupling protein 1 (UCP1) in brown adipose tissue (BAT) for non-shivering thermogenesis"
  ]
}

^["cellular_hydration_and_membrane_potentials"]{
  electrochemical_engines: "The sodium-potassium pump (Na+/K+-ATPase) consuming upwards of 30% of total basal cellular ATP expenditure."
  vital_gradients: #[
    "Intracellular Potassium vs Extracellular Sodium: Maintaining high intracellular K+ (140 mM) and high extracellular Na+ (140 mM) for nerve impulse conduction",
    "Electrolyte Synergy: Water absorption in the small intestine requires sodium-glucose co-transporters (SGLT1); plain water without minerals fails to hydrate deeply",
    "Magnesium Modulation: Regulating intracellular calcium efflux to allow cardiac and skeletal muscle relaxation after contraction"
  ]
}

^["taste"]{
  ~#taste: "Metabolic health is not a punishment of self-denial and calorie deprivation; it is the ecstatic alignment of daily living with the billion-year rhythms of the sun."
  ~#wonder: "Why does fifteen minutes of dawn sunlight in the eyes protect cardiovascular endothelial function twelve hours later when sleep begins?"

  principles: #[
    "Light is biological information: Photons carry molecular signaling instructions just as potent as pharmaceutical drugs.",
    "Rhythm over rigidity: Building a life anchored around consistent waking, feeding, moving, and resting intervals.",
    "Mitochondrial stewardship: Treating the microscopic cellular powerhouses inherited from our mothers with pristine care and nourishment."
  ]
}

^"invariants"{
  "Melatonin synthesis by the pineal gland is profoundly suppressed by exposure to indoor blue-wavelength artificial light in the evening.",
  "Skeletal muscle is the primary organ of postprandial glucose disposal, responsible for over 80% of systemic glucose clearance.",
  "Deep slow-wave sleep is essential for intracranial glymphatic clearance and cannot be recovered through fragmented nap architecture.",
}

#>wonder_physio_circadian_metabolic_1
?["How does morning outdoor sunlight exposure compare to pharmacological sleep aids in improving slow-wave sleep depth and next-day insulin sensitivity?"]{
  #:depth #!biological ~#lens(photoperiodic_endocrinology)
  ~#hypothesis: "Twenty minutes of morning sunlight within 30 minutes of waking increases N3 slow-wave sleep duration by 22 minutes and improves HOMA-IR insulin sensitivity by 18% compared to zolpidem administration."
  !probe{ "Conduct crossover clinical study in insomniac adults comparing morning sunlight phototherapy (30 min) against standard hypnotic pharmacotherapy." }
  $%[sleep.slow_wave_n3_minutes, metabolic.homa_ir_delta]
}
